# NO TRAILING SLASH, and that is the whole of a defect this repo shipped.
# `node_modules/` matches a DIRECTORY. On 16 Oct a worktree used for running
# shards in parallel had node_modules symlinked into it, `git add -A` saw a
# SYMLINK rather than a directory, the pattern did not match, and a link
# pointing at its own path was committed and merged. A fresh clone then had a
# self-referential symlink where the packages go, and npx exited silently
# against it. Without the slash the name is matched however it is spelled.
node_modules
test-results/
playwright-report/

# The hand-over backup zips are built fresh for each branch and belong in
# the chat, not in the history: one got swept in by a `git add -A` and was
# half a megabyte of the repo for three commits.
*-backup.zip
